            <fullName>rank_portfolio_risks_179We000000q4xC</fullName>
            <description>Portfolio-level competing-grant risk. Ranks governed Headroom scopes (category + country + fiscal year) across the current scenario by collision risk, tightest headroom, or most competition — for questions like &apos;where are our biggest competing-grant risks?&apos;, &apos;which countries have the tightest Core Program headroom?&apos;, &apos;show me the top 10 headroom collision risks&apos;. Optional category/country/fiscalYear filters and topN.</description>
            <developerName>rank_portfolio_risks_179We000000q4xC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizePortfolioRisks</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>rank_portfolio_risks</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Rank Portfolio Risks</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>get_opportunity_context_179We000000q4xC</fullName>
            <description>Resolves a named grant&apos;s eligible country and program from its Restriction, plus the year, so a competing-grants analysis can run off it. Returns found=true with a single country and program only when the grant resolves to exactly one of each; otherwise found=false and the summary asks which to use.</description>
            <developerName>get_opportunity_context_179We000000q4xC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeGetOpportunityContext</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>get_opportunity_context</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Get Opportunity Context</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>find_competing_grants_179We000000q4xC</fullName>
            <description>Governed competing-grants analysis. Resolves the SAME governed Budget Line population Headroom Analysis uses (Headroom category/program + country + fiscal year) and reports the Opportunities against that population by allocation EXPOSURE (not Opportunity Amount). Returns TWO renderings: &apos;summary&apos; — a concise fundraising answer (secured contributors, pipeline/likely Opportunities, and a short Headroom conclusion) that correctly classifies competition (0 = none, 1 = not yet competing, 2+ = competing) — and &apos;detail&apos; — the full analysis (risk &amp; confidence, why they compete, full Headroom breakdown, what-can-fit, coverage, timing, data quality). Present &apos;summary&apos; by default; use &apos;detail&apos; only on request. Returns found=false for a governed-zero category, a not-yet-configured category, no qualifying lines, or a missing category/country.</description>
            <developerName>find_competing_grants_179We000000q4xC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeFindCompetingGrants</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>find_competing_grants</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Find Competing Grants</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>get_allocations_179We000000q4xC</fullName>
            <description>Funding Allocation drill-down for a governed Headroom scope (category + country + fiscal year). Returns the individual Funding Allocation records grouped by Opportunity and split into Secured vs Likely/Pipeline, with a lead count/total and clickable Allocation, Opportunity, Restriction, Gift Commitment and Budget Line links. Reuses the same governed Budget Line population as find_competing_grants, so totals reconcile. Optional filters: allocationType, allocationStatus, opportunityName; startIndex pages lists longer than 15. Use this the moment the user asks to SEE the underlying allocations.</description>
            <developerName>get_allocations_179We000000q4xC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeGetAllocations</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>get_allocations</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Get Allocations</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>analyze_opportunity_competition_179We000000q4xC</fullName>
            <description>Opportunity-start competition. Given a grant name, finds the Budget Lines its allocations touch, determines the governed Headroom scopes those belong to, and reports the OTHER opportunities competing for the same governed headroom in EACH scope (a multi-scope grant is analyzed per scope, never collapsed), with the focus grant&apos;s exposure per scope and clickable record links. Returns found=false when the grant is not found, is ambiguous, or has no allocations tied to a governed Budget Line.</description>
            <developerName>analyze_opportunity_competition_179We000000q4xC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeOpportunityCompetition</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>analyze_opportunity_competition</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Analyze Opportunity Competition</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>get_funding_context_179We000000q4xC</fullName>
            <description>Traces the funding lineage/relationships around a starting point and returns a decision-ready summary. Two directions: (1) a Budget Line scope (country + business unit, optionally fiscal year and the cost dimensions) returns what funds it — the linked allocations, restrictions, gift commitments, opportunities and donors, with headroom and competing insight; (2) a named grant (opportunityName) returns where that grant&apos;s funding is allocated — the Budget Lines it funds, using allocation amounts, not the whole opportunity amount. Reports missing links (e.g. no gift commitment) instead of guessing.</description>
            <developerName>get_funding_context_179We000000q4xC</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeGetFundingContext</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>get_funding_context</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Get Funding Context</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
